# Temporary ignore — no fixed spring-webmvc has been published on the Spring Framework 6.x line.
#
# Trivy flags org.springframework:spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (managed by the spring-boot 3.5.16
# parent, our newest available 3.5.x) for CVE-2026-47884 and names the fix as 7.0.9 — Spring
# Framework 7.x, which requires Spring Boot 4 (a major, incompatible bump, not something to do
# as a side effect of a story). Confirmed via maven-metadata.xml: 6.2.19 is the latest published
# version on the 6.x line (6.2.20 404s on Maven Central); there is nothing to bump to within our
# current Boot major.
#
# The underlying flaw is RCE via improper path limitation in Spring's XsltView — confirmed NOT
# reachable in this app: `grep -rn "XsltView" src/main/java` returns zero matches, so unlike the
# tomcat-embed-core entries above this isn't even latent, it's an unused code path. Added by
# skillars-deferred-144 with the project owner's explicit sign-off (2026-10-06). REMOVE the
# moment a 6.2.x (or whatever 6.x line the Boot parent moves to) fix ships, or if this app ever
# starts using XsltView (re-evaluate reachability first).
#
# spring-webmvc: Remote Code Execution via improper path limitation in XsltView
CVE-2026-47884

# Temporary ignore — same situation as CVE-2026-47884 immediately above: no fixed spring-webmvc
# has been published on the Spring Framework 6.x line.
#
# Trivy flags org.springframework:spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (same managed version, same spring-boot
# 3.5.16 parent) for CVE-2026-47890 and names the fix as 7.0.9 — Spring Framework 7.x, same major,
# incompatible Boot-4 bump as above. Confirmed via maven-metadata.xml (as of this entry):
# 6.2.19 is still the latest published version on the 6.x line; there is nothing to bump to within
# our current Boot major. Spring's own advisory separately confirms a 6.2.x backport exists only
# for Spring Enterprise Support customers (6.2.20), not on the public Maven Central line we pull
# from.
#
# The underlying flaw is CRLF injection causing SSE stream corruption, but ONLY when an SSE
# response also streams a rendered Spring MVC VIEW FRAGMENT (Thymeleaf-style fragment rendering
# interleaved with Server-Sent Events) — confirmed NOT reachable in this app: this codebase's SSE
# endpoints (VideoSseService/BookingSseService/MessagingEmitterRegistry and their @RestController
# callers) all emit plain data events directly via SseEmitter, never a rendered view/fragment, and
# `grep -rn "ModelAndView\|Fragment" src/main/java` returns zero matches anywhere near them. This
# app's only Thymeleaf-adjacent HTML lives under src/main/resources/mails/ (email templates
# processed outside Spring MVC's view-resolution layer entirely) — Boot's own ThymeleafAutoConfiguration
# even logs "Cannot find template location: classpath:/templates/" at startup, confirming zero
# MVC-resolvable templates exist for a view fragment to ever be rendered from. Added during the
# review-eligibility/coach-photo bug-fix PR (#262) with the project owner's explicit sign-off
# (2026-10-08). REMOVE the moment a 6.2.x (or whatever 6.x line the Boot parent moves to) fix
# ships, or if this app ever starts combining SSE with rendered view fragments (re-evaluate
# reachability first).
#
# spring-webmvc: Stream corruption / CRLF injection in SSE responses that render view fragments
CVE-2026-47890
